            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at Lagoon Complex Sunset Town",
            "review_text": "Анна Фомина\nSt. Petersburg, Russia6 contributions\n0\nTasteful deception\nJan 2026 • Family\nThe interior is acceptable, but the service, the quality of the food, the bathroom is a nightmare. The food order was simple, the kid had fries and orange juice, himself shrimp in a bucket and beer. The shrimp was brought in, well, you were smart enough to split them in half with your hands, and it turned out they were cooked with your head and your head was green brains! It's the way it is, they told me. Are you serious? You bite a closed cellar and you don't know it's got a head. Okay, redone. But the cherry on the cake was a check... 5% service is ok, I understand (but when I got shrimp and baby potatoes, we didn't get napkins and forks) 10% - tax on beer (even though they have it above average price) well and 8% for visa surgery. I pay cash, why do I have to pay 8%? There are two taxes on the menu, but nothing about the third. What they told me was a restaurant rule. How am I supposed to know about them? With all my heart I wish the restaurant to close as soon as possible, they have no future with this attitude.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten January 22, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
